# s3_keybuf_measured
#
# donor      BumbleBee b4_slice_budget_64m (hardcoded budget corrected against the run); same shape as
#            s2_commbuf_measured; here corrected against a number the program prints.
# basis      s2_commbuf_measured host peak:
#              23622.3 MB  95.5%  heap:sigma.cu:242:main  <- gpu_mem.cu:77:cpuMalloc
#                547.6 MB   2.2%  heap:bert.h:89:GPUBERT<unsigned long>::GPUBERT
#                 75.5 MB   0.3%  file:nvidiactl
#            sigma.cu:242 = new SIGMAKeygen<u64>(party, bw, scale, "", keyBufSz): three pinned cpuMalloc
#            allocations:
#              keyBuf      keyBufSz = 20 * OneGB   21474.8 MB
#              llamaBuf1              1 * OneGB     1073.7 MB
#              dummyBuf1              1 * OneGB     1073.7 MB
#                                                  23622.3 MB   <- the published row exactly
# residency  cpuMalloc(size_t, bool pin = true) calls cudaHostRegister; backend/sigma.h:289 passes one
#            argument: every reserved page resident.
# need       steps/s2_commbuf_measured/attrib/resident/run1/party0.log:
#              SNNI_BUF|keybuf_used=18075947008|keybuf_alloc=21474836480     16.83 of 20.00 GiB, 84.2%
#            3.17 GiB pinned, never written.
# lever      keyBufSz 20 * OneGB -> 18 * OneGB, bert-base branch only (model=bert-base n_seq=128
#            n_layer=12 n_head=12 n_embd=768 bw=50 scale=12); other seven branches unchanged.
#
# impl_lever: patches/patch_keybuf_measured.py
# The one lever of this step.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: main
# cost_class: free
#
# name       `main` = grouped-table name (peak-objects.md prints heap:sigma.cu:242:main <-
#            gpu_mem.cu:77:cpuMalloc); allocation fixed by the decomposition above.
# free       oversized reservation; pinning 18 GiB is less work than 20.
# margin     6.9% (1.17 GiB left), chosen assuming no bounds check (keySize = keyBuf - startPtr after
#            writing, backend/sigma.h:307). Correction 2026-08-15: close() ends with
#            assert(keySize < keyBufSize), live in the binary (NDEBUG not defined), run before the
#            online phase: an over-tight buffer corrupts the heap and then aborts. Margin more
#            conservative than needed; measurement unaffected.
# measured   n=1 (replicates: 1, MANIFEST), job 46141069:
#              peak host   24,164,104 -> 22,069,572 kB   -2,094,532 kB   -8.67%
#              runtime             29 s wall
#              gate        T1s, bit-identical to s2 (md5 8ad6a7924964f6817280bc286d2b1817 both sides)
#              marker      SNNI_BUF|keybuf_used=18075947008|keybuf_alloc=19327352832   93.5% full now
#            predicted 2,097,152 kB, measured 2,094,532 kB (0.12%): the unwritten tail was resident.
